<title>CANADA: Canada Jan industrial price index falls 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Canada Jan industrial price index falls 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Tuesday</p>
<p>issued the following economic indicators for January.</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL PRODUCT PRICE INDEX   Month-on-Month   Year-on-Year</p>
<p>    Change				 -0.2		 -0.5</p>
<p>					   Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=86)	    129.4     129.6     130.0</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL PRODUCT PRICE INDEX   Month-on-Month   Year-on-Year</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods		 -0.1		 -2.1</p>
<p>    Finished goods		     -0.3		 +2.2</p>
<p>The IPPI reflects the prices producers receive as goods leave their plants.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of economists had forecast that the overall index would remain unchanged in January from December.</p>
<p>(For more information, contact Statistics Canada's Client Services Unit at (613) 951-3350 or fax: (613) 951-2848)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
